1
00:00:05,405 --> 00:00:09,242
It's the Seika era,
in the democratic country of Nipponia.

2
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:13,113
A huge ruling party has held power
for a long time.

3
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:17,350
This once-rich country is now
on the edge of a cliff.

4
00:00:17,951 --> 00:00:20,220
The gap between rich and poor
keeps growing.

5
00:00:20,286 --> 00:00:22,422
Both blue-collar workers
and yakuza have no money.

6
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:24,491
Even thieves have no money to steal.

7
00:00:24,557 --> 00:00:27,660
I am Yayoi "Lupin" Kisaragi!

8
00:00:27,727 --> 00:00:31,431
This great thief's surname is Kisaragi,
her given name is Yayoi.

9
00:00:31,498 --> 00:00:35,702
She's after the Cabinet secret funds
in Nagatanicho,

10
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:37,404
the center of the nation.

11
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:41,141
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office,
there is a big safe.

12
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,710
It's full of money.

13
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:45,812
It's the Cabinet's secret stash.

14
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:50,083
It's used to buy top-secret info,
both at home and abroad.

15
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,986
So no receipts are needed,

16
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:55,855
and they don't have to report
how it was used.

17
00:00:55,922 --> 00:00:57,624
I found my treasure!

18
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:00,393
To get into Nagatanicho,

19
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:03,263
Yayoi recruited a mysterious
information broker, Inui.

20
00:01:03,329 --> 00:01:07,033
Then she approached Miyabi,
daughter of Shiro Kobayakawa,

21
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:10,570
heiress of the glorious
political Kobayakawa family!

22
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:13,473
I will become a Diet Member!

23
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:17,510
Miyabi runs in the new Chiba District 17,

24
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:19,979
which was split
from the Kobayakawa home base.

25
00:01:20,046 --> 00:01:22,715
Her opponent is her own brother, Hayate.

26
00:01:22,782 --> 00:01:24,784
A battle between siblings!

27
00:01:24,851 --> 00:01:27,620
I can't believe they really dissolved it.

28
00:01:27,687 --> 00:01:29,823
I can't take this anymore!

29
00:01:29,889 --> 00:01:31,758
This is Masakado Natsume,

30
00:01:31,825 --> 00:01:34,094
the party's treasurer
and a member of the Upper House.

31
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,329
Hayate has no election experience.

32
00:01:36,396 --> 00:01:38,665
Your support would be reassuring.

33
00:01:38,731 --> 00:01:39,933
I would be glad to help.

34
00:01:39,999 --> 00:01:43,369
Are you perhaps interested in me?

35
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:44,671
Yes, I am.

36
00:01:45,238 --> 00:01:48,842
Oh, I'm happy.

37
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:51,878
A silly battle
between two sly foxes has begun!

38
00:01:52,512 --> 00:01:56,816
What she will steal
is the dark money of politicians!

39
00:01:56,883 --> 00:01:58,451
PoliticaLupin!

40
00:02:01,988 --> 00:02:04,524
FOR SALE

41
00:02:04,591 --> 00:02:05,792
What's this?

42
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:07,560
Remains of dreams.

43
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:10,163
The Jumbo lottery.
Every time, I buy 30 tickets.

44
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:13,766
For the past 20 years,
I've won 81,000 yen.

45
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:16,936
That's a 91% loss.

46
00:02:17,003 --> 00:02:18,304
Basically thrown in a ditch!

47
00:02:18,371 --> 00:02:19,439
A money ditch!

48
00:02:19,506 --> 00:02:22,275
Listen. Elections are about base,
signboard, and bag.

49
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:23,676
The bag is money.

50
00:02:23,743 --> 00:02:26,913
The more money you have, the more likely
your victory. That's reality.

51
00:02:28,014 --> 00:02:29,048
Here.

52
00:02:29,115 --> 00:02:32,418
If you get the ruling party's endorsement,
like your brother,

53
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,653
you get…

54
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,288
JUMBO LOTTERY TICKETS

55
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,423
…20 million yen from the party.

56
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:40,360
Also, you get lots of party members,
support groups,

57
00:02:40,426 --> 00:02:44,230
and over 100 volunteers to help you out.

58
00:02:44,764 --> 00:02:45,899
And what do we have?

59
00:02:48,101 --> 00:02:50,503
A few elites! What about funds?

60
00:02:52,205 --> 00:02:54,207
Here's what I scraped together.

61
00:02:55,208 --> 00:02:57,243
-Three million yen.
-Really?

62
00:02:59,145 --> 00:03:01,214
That's just the deposit!

63
00:03:01,281 --> 00:03:02,615
I thought you were rich?

64
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:04,784
My parents are. I have no cash.

65
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,286
We have no time! Let's take some photos!

66
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,353
All right.

67
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:10,857
Nice! Lovely! Perfect!

68
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:13,927
Turn your body a little. Face the front.

69
00:03:13,993 --> 00:03:14,961
Excuse me.

70
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,863
-Stay still.
-A little more this way. Okay.

71
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,032
Open up the chest a little.

72
00:03:19,098 --> 00:03:21,501
Relax! And now smile.

73
00:03:21,568 --> 00:03:24,470
Okay, smile!

74
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:25,705
-Great!
-Three!

75
00:03:25,772 --> 00:03:27,607
Two! One!

76
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:31,511
HAYATE KOBAYAKAWA

77
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:39,352
The Kokuji Party's endorsed candidate,
Hayate Kobayakawa!

78
00:03:39,419 --> 00:03:41,487
Hayate Kobayakawa, everyone!

79
00:03:42,322 --> 00:03:45,692
A new wind for the Kokuji Party,
Hayate Kobayakawa!

80
00:03:45,758 --> 00:03:49,662
Hayate Kobayakawa, everyone! Thank you!

81
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:52,665
Please support Hayate Kobayakawa!

82
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:53,633
HAYATE KOBAYAKAWA

83
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:54,968
-Please support us.
-Thank you!

84
00:03:55,034 --> 00:03:56,836
Thank you. Excuse me.

85
00:03:57,971 --> 00:03:59,872
It's finally starting!

86
00:03:59,939 --> 00:04:02,275
That health insurance scandal…

87
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:03,576
What's with that?

88
00:04:03,643 --> 00:04:05,478
It's certainly wrong.

89
00:04:05,545 --> 00:04:08,815
If I'm elected, I'll change
the Kokuji party from the inside.

90
00:04:08,881 --> 00:04:10,116
Good luck.

91
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:12,485
-Do your best.
-Thank you.

92
00:04:12,552 --> 00:04:13,686
I'll do all I can.

93
00:04:14,187 --> 00:04:16,256
KOKUJI PARTY

94
00:04:16,322 --> 00:04:19,525
We won't give my daughter
any campaign money.

95
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:21,594
Once she's a candidate,

96
00:04:21,661 --> 00:04:23,162
she's our enemy.

97
00:04:25,898 --> 00:04:28,635
The Chiba Shinyo Bank called.

98
00:04:28,701 --> 00:04:32,071
Your family home
is being taken as collateral.

99
00:04:32,138 --> 00:04:33,072
What?

100
00:04:33,139 --> 00:04:36,776
Miyabi did it to raise campaign funds.

101
00:04:38,211 --> 00:04:40,380
That's our home base!

102
00:04:42,348 --> 00:04:45,451
If you lose, you lose both
the house and land?

103
00:04:45,518 --> 00:04:46,653
Are you fine with that?

104
00:04:46,719 --> 00:04:47,820
Sure.

105
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:51,457
My grandmother left this house to me.

106
00:04:55,728 --> 00:04:56,829
Come in.

107
00:04:57,463 --> 00:05:01,034
-Excuse me…
-So huge…

108
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,268
What…

109
00:05:02,835 --> 00:05:06,205
Mr. Hayate Kobayakawa
is sure to become a politician

110
00:05:06,272 --> 00:05:08,675
who leads Japan's new era!

111
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:15,615
He was raised by Mr. Shiro,

112
00:05:15,682 --> 00:05:19,252
and loves everyone here
in Chiba District 17!

113
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,754
Do your best!

114
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:25,325
I think we can do a few more
campaign tours.

115
00:05:25,892 --> 00:05:29,228
I don't think we need to
cram in that many.

116
00:05:30,496 --> 00:05:32,432
Did the election planner,
Mr. Hayashi, say that?

117
00:05:32,498 --> 00:05:34,100
No. It's my opinion.

118
00:05:36,235 --> 00:05:38,371
Oh, can we stop by my family home?

119
00:05:38,438 --> 00:05:39,439
We don't have time.

120
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,473
Just a moment…

121
00:05:43,643 --> 00:05:44,644
Stop the car!

122
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:53,986
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA

123
00:05:57,957 --> 00:05:59,125
Miyabi!

124
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:04,564
What are you doing?
Put your office somewhere else!

125
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:05,565
Why?

126
00:06:05,631 --> 00:06:07,867
If you do this, then I can't stay here!

127
00:06:07,934 --> 00:06:09,135
Just stay at a hotel.

128
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,403
Why should I?

129
00:06:10,470 --> 00:06:11,704
This is my house.

130
00:06:11,771 --> 00:06:13,206
That's only on paper.

131
00:06:13,272 --> 00:06:14,640
Paper is everything.

132
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:15,742
Shall I make tea?

133
00:06:15,808 --> 00:06:17,276
-No, thanks.
-No need.

134
00:06:17,343 --> 00:06:18,544
Hello.

135
00:06:18,611 --> 00:06:19,445
Hello.

136
00:06:19,512 --> 00:06:20,580
Hello.

137
00:06:21,647 --> 00:06:24,684
I didn't think you would use Mr. Shiro's
family home as an election office.

138
00:06:24,751 --> 00:06:26,219
Can't you tell?

139
00:06:26,285 --> 00:06:28,121
Miyabi is the heiress, it seems.

140
00:06:28,187 --> 00:06:30,189
It's for saving money. We had no choice.

141
00:06:30,256 --> 00:06:31,357
Who's the strategist?

142
00:06:31,424 --> 00:06:32,625
Me.

143
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,799
Appealing to the common people?

144
00:06:40,967 --> 00:06:43,403
A weak independent candidate
with no party backing

145
00:06:43,469 --> 00:06:45,772
needs a desperate measure like this.

146
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:50,977
When the Kobayakawa siblings
fight in this election,

147
00:06:51,043 --> 00:06:52,245
the media will bite.

148
00:06:52,311 --> 00:06:54,814
It's like… an election hack.

149
00:06:58,918 --> 00:06:59,986
Do you think you can win?

150
00:07:02,321 --> 00:07:03,790
I don't know.

151
00:07:03,856 --> 00:07:07,727
The sibling fight is only good
for making the first impact.

152
00:07:07,794 --> 00:07:09,896
We need a story.

153
00:07:09,962 --> 00:07:11,197
For example?

154
00:07:12,064 --> 00:07:15,201
"The little sister used to be
bullied by her brother."

155
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:16,969
Do you think we can win with that?

156
00:07:17,036 --> 00:07:19,405
Voters like strength and intelligence,

157
00:07:19,472 --> 00:07:21,541
but Miyabi has neither.

158
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:24,076
She has approachability.
So we need a story.

159
00:07:24,143 --> 00:07:26,579
One that would make everyone
want to vote for her.

160
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:33,152
A poor little girl who bravely opposes
her bigwig father and brother.

161
00:07:37,023 --> 00:07:38,291
I don't like that.

162
00:07:38,357 --> 00:07:39,559
Don't be picky.

163
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:40,693
It's too dark!

164
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,795
Don't say it as if I'm the dark one.

165
00:07:46,265 --> 00:07:49,335
How about, "Pitiful but in a healthy way"?

166
00:07:51,904 --> 00:07:52,972
Hello!

167
00:07:53,039 --> 00:07:56,242
This is new candidate Miyabi Kobayakawa.

168
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,143
Hello.

169
00:07:57,210 --> 00:07:59,712
She's running
for the House of Representatives.

170
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:01,881
Miyabi Kobayakawa!

171
00:08:01,948 --> 00:08:03,149
Hello.

172
00:08:03,216 --> 00:08:05,218
Please support her!

173
00:08:05,284 --> 00:08:08,020
-Found a board!
-Yeah.

174
00:08:10,356 --> 00:08:11,290
All right.

175
00:08:11,357 --> 00:08:13,125
-I'll put it up.
-Yeah.

176
00:08:13,192 --> 00:08:14,627
Okay.

177
00:08:18,197 --> 00:08:19,832
TO CREATE FAIR POLITICS
WITH NO COLLUSION!

178
00:08:24,871 --> 00:08:26,939
Sorry for making a ruckus. Hello.

179
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,908
-Please support us.
-Please.

180
00:08:28,975 --> 00:08:30,076
It's so hot!

181
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,944
Drink some water.

182
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:32,945
Thank you!

183
00:08:33,613 --> 00:08:36,382
Hello! I'm Miyabi Kobayakawa.

184
00:08:36,449 --> 00:08:37,416
Hello.

185
00:08:42,588 --> 00:08:43,789
All right.

186
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:46,726
-Please support us.
-Okay.

187
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:50,796
Miyabi Kobayakawa is putting up posters!

188
00:08:50,863 --> 00:08:52,164
The person herself!

189
00:08:52,231 --> 00:08:53,165
Hello.

190
00:08:53,232 --> 00:08:54,967
Please support us!

191
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,736
-Do your best!
-Thank you!

192
00:08:56,802 --> 00:08:58,538
-I'm rooting for you!
-Do your best!

193
00:08:58,604 --> 00:08:59,572
Please support us.

194
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:02,842
Miyabi Kobayakawa is putting up posters!

195
00:09:02,909 --> 00:09:04,810
Please support us!

196
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:05,811
Okay.

197
00:09:06,312 --> 00:09:08,748
TEN DAYS UNTIL VOTING DAY

198
00:09:15,588 --> 00:09:17,590
DISTRICT 17 - MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA
INDEPENDENT

199
00:09:17,657 --> 00:09:18,758
I'M PUTTING UP POSTERS

200
00:09:18,824 --> 00:09:21,627
I have no campaign funds,
so I borrowed money.

201
00:09:21,694 --> 00:09:25,398
I have no car, so I run
and put up posters along the way.

202
00:09:25,932 --> 00:09:28,768
I have decent stamina. Please support me!

203
00:09:28,834 --> 00:09:30,002
I'm off!

204
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,370
IS THIS A PUNISHMENT GAME?

205
00:09:31,437 --> 00:09:33,105
THE ELECTION WILL BE OVER
BY THE TIME SHE'S DONE

206
00:09:33,172 --> 00:09:34,340
BOTH CUTE AND PITIFUL

207
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:35,408
Let's go!

208
00:09:35,474 --> 00:09:38,344
-Thank you!
-Thank you so much!

209
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,680
-In this heat…
-Impressive!

210
00:09:42,982 --> 00:09:44,417
Okay.

211
00:09:44,483 --> 00:09:46,385
-Please drink this.
-Thank you!

212
00:09:46,452 --> 00:09:47,520
Thank you.

213
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:50,356
Back then, you used to attend Mr. Ichiro
and Mr. Shiro's speeches, right?

214
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:51,257
Yes!

215
00:09:51,324 --> 00:09:52,592
How you've grown!

216
00:09:52,658 --> 00:09:53,893
I'm 166 cm.

217
00:09:54,727 --> 00:09:56,896
-Good luck.
-Thank you!

218
00:09:56,963 --> 00:09:59,565
-I'll do my best.
-Thank you.

219
00:09:59,632 --> 00:10:01,067
Miyabi Kobayakawa!

220
00:10:01,133 --> 00:10:02,134
Please support us!

221
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:04,370
A new wind for the Kokuji Party,

222
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:07,306
endorsed candidate Hayate Kobayakawa!

223
00:10:07,373 --> 00:10:11,210
Hayate Kobayakawa! Thank you!

224
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:14,013
Sorry for the loud mic behind you.

225
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:17,850
We wish
candidate Miyabi Kobayakawa good luck.

226
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:20,419
A new wind for the Kokuji Party,

227
00:10:20,486 --> 00:10:23,389
endorsed candidate Hayate Kobayakawa!

228
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:27,059
Hayate Kobayakawa! Thank you!

229
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,528
Sorry for the loud mic behind you.

230
00:10:29,595 --> 00:10:31,330
-So hot.
-Welcome back.

231
00:10:31,397 --> 00:10:32,231
Welcome back.

232
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:33,132
Thank you.

233
00:10:33,199 --> 00:10:34,767
Welcome back.

234
00:10:34,834 --> 00:10:36,469
Hey. You're back early.

235
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:39,939
I cut it short.

236
00:10:40,573 --> 00:10:42,541
It's so hot…

237
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:51,417
You should do more stationary speeches.

238
00:10:52,018 --> 00:10:53,285
No way…

239
00:10:54,253 --> 00:10:57,056
People will have
to stand in the heat and listen.

240
00:10:59,225 --> 00:11:01,160
I'll win either way.

241
00:11:04,930 --> 00:11:07,967
CANDIDATE SUPPORT RATES

242
00:11:08,034 --> 00:11:11,137
HAYATE - 41% SUPPORT
MIYABI - 19% SUPPORT

243
00:11:20,746 --> 00:11:22,248
Excuse me.

244
00:11:22,815 --> 00:11:23,716
Yes?

245
00:11:25,251 --> 00:11:26,152
Yes?

246
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:29,288
Hey, may we help you put up posters?

247
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,090
-Are you sure?
-Yes!

248
00:11:31,157 --> 00:11:32,124
Thank you!

249
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:35,027
People often say
"taking over the family business,"

250
00:11:35,094 --> 00:11:37,463
but is politics a family business?

251
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,965
It concerns the whole country, after all.

252
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:44,704
Nipponia is a parliamentary
democracy with no class system.

253
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:45,638
Supposedly.

254
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:46,706
But…

255
00:11:46,772 --> 00:11:50,142
But there is still hierarchy
between people, isn't there?

256
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:52,445
Hereditary succession is like that.

257
00:11:52,511 --> 00:11:55,347
The posters and map are inside.
Thank you so much.

258
00:11:55,414 --> 00:11:58,417
-Thank you!
-We're off!

259
00:11:58,484 --> 00:11:59,952
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA

260
00:12:00,019 --> 00:12:01,187
Momo!

261
00:12:01,253 --> 00:12:02,722
You're doing well!

262
00:12:02,788 --> 00:12:03,756
You came here to see me?

263
00:12:03,823 --> 00:12:06,892
After seeing Miyabi running out there,
I couldn't sit still!

264
00:12:06,959 --> 00:12:09,495
Yeah, she is like a celeb now.

265
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:11,230
-Come in!
-Sure.

266
00:12:11,297 --> 00:12:12,832
I'm Saibara.

267
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:16,335
This program brings together candidates
from a district gathering attention,

268
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:18,037
and we're live again today.

269
00:12:18,104 --> 00:12:20,840
District 17 is a hot topic,
because of the sibling rivalry.

270
00:12:22,007 --> 00:12:24,443
The man in the middle,
Mr. Hachimaki, is also independent.

271
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:27,680
The opposition parties
didn't even field candidates here,

272
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:30,683
because this is called
the "Kobayakawa Kingdom."

273
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,852
Anyone but the Kokuji Party
is a sure loser here.

274
00:12:34,153 --> 00:12:36,822
Miyabi, why do you run in District 17?

275
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:40,993
I lived here with my grandparents
until middle school.

276
00:12:41,827 --> 00:12:45,397
Your pledge
is to abolish hereditary politics,

277
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:49,101
but running in the Kobayakawa Kingdom
is close to inheriting, isn't it?

278
00:12:49,168 --> 00:12:53,005
I'm not getting any support
from my father or the party.

279
00:12:53,572 --> 00:12:55,808
But you're a politician's child.

280
00:12:55,875 --> 00:13:00,045
It's not that politicians' children
must not become politicians.

281
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:04,683
It's unfair that children
automatically inherit a base,

282
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:06,786
and that this has become normal.

283
00:13:06,852 --> 00:13:08,788
As such, it must be abolished.

284
00:13:08,854 --> 00:13:13,125
Of course, everyone can choose
to run for elections if they want to.

285
00:13:13,759 --> 00:13:16,962
Hayate, you inherited the base.
Your response?

286
00:13:17,029 --> 00:13:19,498
I'm not sure this is a response,

287
00:13:20,065 --> 00:13:24,003
but however much she acts like a commoner,
my sister is a Kobayakawa.

288
00:13:24,069 --> 00:13:27,673
She even ran around on the streets
just to garner popularity.

289
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:29,275
She's pretending to be common folk.

290
00:13:29,341 --> 00:13:31,277
It's worse because she hides it.

291
00:13:31,343 --> 00:13:35,648
She's part of the class system
that she herself wants to abolish.

292
00:13:35,714 --> 00:13:38,284
You sound harsh. Are you on bad terms?

293
00:13:38,350 --> 00:13:39,218
Not at all.

294
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:43,489
No. Back then, she was adorable
and followed me around.

295
00:13:43,556 --> 00:13:46,325
She cried saying that studying was hard,

296
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:48,360
and I taught her each time.

297
00:13:49,128 --> 00:13:51,430
Well, she's a girl, after all.

298
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:53,699
Girls are allowed to be that spoiled.

299
00:13:55,868 --> 00:13:59,705
Bro, in high school,
you came crying to me, too.

300
00:13:59,772 --> 00:14:02,007
"I might have gotten my girlfriend
pregnant, what do I do?"

301
00:14:02,074 --> 00:14:06,045
It shocked me that you and Dad
only talked about how to hide it,

302
00:14:06,111 --> 00:14:08,247
not worrying about the girl.

303
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:10,716
She wasn't pregnant in the end, but…

304
00:14:10,783 --> 00:14:14,053
You were in the news
for causing trouble at a host club!

305
00:14:14,119 --> 00:14:15,654
Who cleaned that up?

306
00:14:15,721 --> 00:14:16,789
I didn't ask you to.

307
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:19,158
You got drunk, vomited on the street,
and got photographed.

308
00:14:19,225 --> 00:14:20,693
People puke, you know.

309
00:14:20,759 --> 00:14:23,062
-Don't say "puke."
-You brought it up first!

310
00:14:23,128 --> 00:14:24,463
No, I didn't say "puke."

311
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,564
You just did.

312
00:14:27,066 --> 00:14:28,000
Maybe emesis?

313
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:32,071
Emesis? Why are you getting
all medical here?

314
00:14:36,275 --> 00:14:37,576
You two are in sync.

315
00:14:37,643 --> 00:14:39,211
-No, we're not!
-No, we're not!

316
00:14:40,579 --> 00:14:43,549
Let's end the sibling talk

317
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:46,318
and move on to each of your policies.

318
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:48,954
Who would like to go first?

319
00:14:49,021 --> 00:14:50,656
It's so over.

320
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:53,559
They both look good on video.

321
00:14:57,529 --> 00:14:59,531
It's your fault
for saying unnecessary things.

322
00:14:59,598 --> 00:15:01,500
You were annoying too.

323
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,435
You were pretty mean.

324
00:15:03,502 --> 00:15:05,237
True, he was unprofessional.

325
00:15:05,304 --> 00:15:07,306
Natsume, you're on her side?

326
00:15:07,373 --> 00:15:09,842
That was not an attitude
you should use in formal events.

327
00:15:10,342 --> 00:15:13,879
It's weird that I have to debate my sister
in the first place.

328
00:15:13,946 --> 00:15:18,217
Why do you have to run in my district?
Run somewhere else.

329
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:21,420
Do you hold a grudge against me?

330
00:15:24,523 --> 00:15:26,892
You cried
in your third year of middle school.

331
00:15:27,793 --> 00:15:30,296
Before summer vacation,
your grades dropped.

332
00:15:30,362 --> 00:15:33,032
Dad said that you had promised to study,

333
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:35,167
and made you throw out your things.

334
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:54,620
I can't forget it. That was cruel.

335
00:15:55,888 --> 00:15:58,590
You don't have to listen to Dad, you know?

336
00:16:02,895 --> 00:16:05,631
I remember the time you cried too.

337
00:16:07,066 --> 00:16:09,969
ROUSSEAU
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

338
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:28,887
What is Miyabi doing?

339
00:16:28,954 --> 00:16:31,056
She doesn't even help around the house!

340
00:16:36,895 --> 00:16:38,630
Hey, Grandma, listen.

341
00:16:39,498 --> 00:16:42,234
"Man is born free,

342
00:16:42,301 --> 00:16:45,571
but everywhere he is in chains."

343
00:16:45,637 --> 00:16:46,905
Deep, right?

344
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:52,144
To stay free, we need a social contract.

345
00:16:52,211 --> 00:16:54,313
This idea of popular sovereignty

346
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,715
led to our Constitution.

347
00:16:59,084 --> 00:17:01,220
JEAN-JACQUES ROUSSEAU
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

348
00:17:03,489 --> 00:17:05,157
You don't have to read this.

349
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:10,696
I want to be a politician.

350
00:17:10,763 --> 00:17:14,066
A job to improve the country.
It sounds fun.

351
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:17,403
And if I take over the family business,
big bro can make games.

352
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:20,506
Listen, Miyabi.

353
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,876
Your grandfather and father

354
00:17:24,643 --> 00:17:27,846
dislike women who become politicians.

355
00:17:28,414 --> 00:17:29,882
You understand?

356
00:17:37,923 --> 00:17:39,725
If only our positions were reversed…

357
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:42,561
That's what I thought.

358
00:17:44,863 --> 00:17:48,267
Don't mind me, but give up
trying to beat the Kobayakawa family.

359
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:52,471
You'll lose.
We have money and people behind us.

360
00:17:52,538 --> 00:17:54,273
-Hayate.
-I have to be blunt!

361
00:17:54,339 --> 00:17:55,441
She understands nothing.

362
00:18:02,347 --> 00:18:08,620
The head of my law office
is elderly, and he retired

363
00:18:08,687 --> 00:18:10,456
and closed down the law firm.

364
00:18:10,522 --> 00:18:15,294
So I decided to run in the elections,
to change society through law.

365
00:18:16,195 --> 00:18:20,099
I was just on an online talkshow,

366
00:18:20,732 --> 00:18:23,335
but I couldn't say anything.

367
00:18:23,402 --> 00:18:26,238
INDEPENDENT
HACHIMAKI

368
00:18:26,305 --> 00:18:29,575
I couldn't say anything at all.

369
00:18:29,641 --> 00:18:30,909
You'll be fine!

370
00:18:30,976 --> 00:18:32,077
Do your best!

371
00:18:32,144 --> 00:18:34,279
Thank you! I'll do all I can.

372
00:18:37,349 --> 00:18:38,851
Before the campaign,

373
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:41,687
Mr. Kiuchi came by.

374
00:18:42,554 --> 00:18:44,456
I got Suzuran hamburger rice crackers.

375
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:45,891
Hamburger crackers?

376
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,460
They are a long-time supporter
of Mr. Shiro's.

377
00:18:49,595 --> 00:18:51,763
Did you come all this way to see me?

378
00:18:51,830 --> 00:18:55,167
Well, it's work. I have to give
all prefectural party members…

379
00:18:56,034 --> 00:18:57,469
Our "seasonal greeting."

380
00:18:57,536 --> 00:19:00,139
A "seasonal greeting"?

381
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,007
What is that?

382
00:19:06,111 --> 00:19:08,147
What? Is something wrong?

383
00:19:08,947 --> 00:19:11,683
Please tell me.
I want to learn everything.

384
00:19:12,751 --> 00:19:16,588
This is our seasonal greeting. Thank you.

385
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:19,691
Thank you. Thank you.

386
00:19:19,758 --> 00:19:23,695
I heard from Kiuchi. Hayate got angry?

387
00:19:23,762 --> 00:19:25,564
Not really angry…

388
00:19:27,332 --> 00:19:29,801
More like shocked.

389
00:19:30,302 --> 00:19:34,173
In an election race,
money flies in stacks of cash.

390
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:37,276
That's just how things work.

391
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,745
Sorry to ask, Natsume…

392
00:19:39,811 --> 00:19:40,879
Yes?

393
00:19:40,946 --> 00:19:43,015
Please talk some sense into him.

394
00:20:03,502 --> 00:20:04,903
In elections, we need

395
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:08,840
support from prefectural
and city assembly members.

396
00:20:08,907 --> 00:20:11,610
They ask local companies and residents

397
00:20:11,677 --> 00:20:15,681
to vote for you and gather the votes.

398
00:20:15,747 --> 00:20:19,117
And this is the "reward."

399
00:20:19,184 --> 00:20:20,519
That's election fraud, isn't it?

400
00:20:21,753 --> 00:20:23,789
True, you can't do it
during the election itself.

401
00:20:23,855 --> 00:20:26,024
Even before the election it's still fraud.

402
00:20:26,091 --> 00:20:27,960
It's only fraud if you say "Vote for me."

403
00:20:28,026 --> 00:20:30,762
It's just "thanks for your help"
and giving them cash?

404
00:20:30,829 --> 00:20:32,431
That's what's going on, right?

405
00:20:32,497 --> 00:20:34,366
Neither side says anything.

406
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:37,402
It's an unspoken understanding,
so it isn't fraud.

407
00:20:37,469 --> 00:20:39,071
-But that's…
-But that's…

408
00:20:39,571 --> 00:20:40,472
It's wrong.

409
00:20:41,273 --> 00:20:42,474
I said so too.

410
00:20:42,541 --> 00:20:45,210
What if I were to expose that,
like what I did today?

411
00:20:45,277 --> 00:20:46,812
You've got no proof!

412
00:20:47,879 --> 00:20:49,548
Even I saw nothing.

413
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,517
No one will admit they received any money.

414
00:20:53,118 --> 00:20:55,921
And we won't say,
"We gave them money" either.

415
00:20:56,488 --> 00:20:58,790
Is that how you became
a Diet member, Mr. Natsume?

416
00:21:03,528 --> 00:21:05,197
Luckily for me,

417
00:21:07,032 --> 00:21:10,369
a retiring senior member recommended me,

418
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,671
so I got his supporters.

419
00:21:12,738 --> 00:21:16,108
It wasn't a tough fight,
so there was no money to hand out.

420
00:21:16,174 --> 00:21:20,579
I was lucky to get the endorsement.

421
00:21:20,646 --> 00:21:23,215
Not every election depends on money.

422
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:25,851
But in my District 17,
money was being handed out.

423
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,620
If it was you, Mr. Natsume,

424
00:21:29,187 --> 00:21:30,822
would you just quietly go along?

425
00:21:32,257 --> 00:21:36,795
I'm not going to be Prime Minister.
I just hold a small seat.

426
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:42,034
I can't imagine what it's like
to be in your position.

427
00:21:46,605 --> 00:21:48,340
In the end,

428
00:21:49,675 --> 00:21:51,109
you must decide for yourself.

429
00:21:59,785 --> 00:22:02,688
It's hard being a Diet member.

430
00:22:03,255 --> 00:22:04,623
What do you mean?

431
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:08,260
The money being handed out.

432
00:22:10,729 --> 00:22:12,364
I mean, I don't blame you.

433
00:22:12,898 --> 00:22:15,133
That's how the world is nowadays.

434
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:19,504
Is that money party grants? Donations?

435
00:22:19,571 --> 00:22:20,939
Or… Cabinet secret funds?

436
00:22:22,541 --> 00:22:24,376
Well, it's probably dirty money, anyway.

437
00:22:24,443 --> 00:22:28,480
With all due respect,
it's not necessarily dirty money.

438
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:33,151
If the party branch issues a receipt

439
00:22:33,218 --> 00:22:37,322
and the member records it as a donation
in the political funds report, it's legal.

440
00:22:37,389 --> 00:22:39,257
Did you issue a receipt?

441
00:22:40,325 --> 00:22:41,927
When you're about to be exposed,

442
00:22:41,993 --> 00:22:44,863
you issue a receipt after the fact
and record it.

443
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:47,065
The report is released over a year later.

444
00:22:47,132 --> 00:22:49,201
The election will be long over then.

445
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:54,172
That's a very convenient rule!

446
00:22:58,510 --> 00:22:59,511
Excuse me.

447
00:23:02,514 --> 00:23:05,484
Wow, you're so good at this!

448
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,085
Thank you!

449
00:23:13,825 --> 00:23:15,727
Everyone, I'm sorry.

450
00:23:17,295 --> 00:23:20,198
You all worked hard with me, but I…

451
00:23:21,933 --> 00:23:23,335
Clumsy me!

452
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:25,971
It's because of the heat!
This summer is so hot!

453
00:23:26,538 --> 00:23:28,774
We're done for today. See you tomorrow.

454
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,143
Thank you for today.

455
00:23:31,209 --> 00:23:33,245
See you tomorrow. Take care.

456
00:23:33,311 --> 00:23:34,212
See you.

457
00:23:34,279 --> 00:23:35,881
-Thank you!
-Thank you very much.

458
00:23:35,947 --> 00:23:37,516
Be careful on the way home!

459
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:39,451
Thank you for today.
Please take care.

460
00:23:39,518 --> 00:23:40,786
Good work.

461
00:23:40,852 --> 00:23:43,388
-We're going home already?
-Why?

462
00:23:43,455 --> 00:23:45,290
What's wrong?

463
00:23:45,357 --> 00:23:46,992
Getting sick of each other?

464
00:23:47,058 --> 00:23:49,361
Why are you here all of a sudden?

465
00:23:50,328 --> 00:23:53,064
You went viral. In a bad way.

466
00:23:53,632 --> 00:23:54,699
Huh?

467
00:23:57,636 --> 00:23:59,504
I'm running in this election!

468
00:24:00,205 --> 00:24:03,275
Everything is because of summer!

469
00:24:04,509 --> 00:24:06,378
People puke, you know.

470
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:08,213
Don't say "puke."

471
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,214
SPENT TONS OF MONEY
ON A HOST, THEN GOT DUMPED

472
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:10,649
GETTING DRUNK AND VOMITING

473
00:24:11,349 --> 00:24:13,151
IDIOT DAUGHTER OF THE KOBAYAKAWAS

474
00:24:13,218 --> 00:24:14,319
STUPID SPOILED GIRL

475
00:24:14,386 --> 00:24:15,620
NO CURE FOR STUPIDITY

476
00:24:15,687 --> 00:24:17,856
STUPID WOMAN

477
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:19,524
I HATE POLITICIANS LIKE THIS

478
00:24:24,396 --> 00:24:26,798
Don't read this stuff.
It will poison your mind.

479
00:24:28,934 --> 00:24:31,770
Your brother's talk was awful too.

480
00:24:31,837 --> 00:24:33,872
-True.
-Right?

481
00:24:33,939 --> 00:24:37,108
But his side has an ad agency
handling the internet.

482
00:24:37,175 --> 00:24:40,011
How much are they spending?
Is there a spending cap?

483
00:24:40,078 --> 00:24:41,046
No.

484
00:24:41,112 --> 00:24:42,280
Why?

485
00:24:42,347 --> 00:24:44,950
I tried, but it was pointless.

486
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,586
I feel stupid.

487
00:24:49,054 --> 00:24:51,523
Well, I'm a stupid woman, so it's natural.

488
00:24:53,225 --> 00:24:56,495
In the end, it's all about money.
How frustrating.

489
00:24:59,097 --> 00:25:01,466
Yes, it's all about money.

490
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:04,002
The world runs on money.

491
00:25:05,403 --> 00:25:07,873
Don't get scared
just because some people mocked you.

492
00:25:07,939 --> 00:25:10,075
Don't be whining just yet.

493
00:25:11,543 --> 00:25:14,212
You mortgaged this house
and borrowed money.

494
00:25:14,279 --> 00:25:15,914
That's a great resolve.

495
00:25:17,282 --> 00:25:18,517
But is it?

496
00:25:19,618 --> 00:25:22,521
If you lose, your dad will just handle it.

497
00:25:22,587 --> 00:25:24,022
He'll help.

498
00:25:24,089 --> 00:25:27,092
He won't let this home base of his
be taken by the bank.

499
00:25:27,158 --> 00:25:28,927
You know that, right?

500
00:25:29,628 --> 00:25:32,898
You haven't thrown anything anyway.

501
00:25:32,964 --> 00:25:34,699
You have everything.

502
00:25:34,766 --> 00:25:38,570
Your brother was right.
You're a spoiled girl who has it all.

503
00:25:40,939 --> 00:25:42,073
But…

504
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:45,210
what about the people
who helped put up posters?

505
00:25:45,911 --> 00:25:47,946
They didn't get a single yen.

506
00:25:48,613 --> 00:25:51,850
They came because they wanted
to support you. What about them?

507
00:25:52,517 --> 00:25:55,086
Will you throw them away? Will you quit?

508
00:25:59,291 --> 00:26:02,994
No one here has money on their mind.

509
00:26:14,005 --> 00:26:15,273
No one here has money on their mind!

510
00:26:16,308 --> 00:26:18,577
I'm not after Miyabi's money.

511
00:26:19,711 --> 00:26:21,313
Look who's talking. A thief.

512
00:26:21,379 --> 00:26:23,348
-I'm a great thief.
-Great!

513
00:26:30,388 --> 00:26:32,257
No need to worry.

514
00:26:32,324 --> 00:26:35,827
If you hear that the opponent is giving
out money behind the scenes,

515
00:26:35,894 --> 00:26:37,362
you would lose confidence.

516
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:39,097
They didn't give out any money.

517
00:26:39,164 --> 00:26:41,533
They absolutely did. I told you about it.

518
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:44,102
The election starts
before the official day of voting.

519
00:26:44,169 --> 00:26:45,470
Yes, I heard.

520
00:26:45,537 --> 00:26:48,873
Even before the start date,
the battle has already begun.

521
00:26:50,909 --> 00:26:51,943
Let me hear it.

522
00:26:52,644 --> 00:26:55,580
There are districts
you absolutely can't lose.

523
00:26:56,247 --> 00:26:59,217
Decisive districts. All parties
will spend big money for them.

524
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:00,385
I see…

525
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:03,021
I got detailed info beforehand,

526
00:27:03,755 --> 00:27:06,424
so I worked before the start date.

527
00:27:07,726 --> 00:27:10,829
First, I had someone visit
the Kokuji Party office

528
00:27:10,895 --> 00:27:13,131
and learn the schedule,
pretending to file a petition.

529
00:27:14,165 --> 00:27:17,002
Wild boars are ruining my fields.

530
00:27:17,068 --> 00:27:18,870
A boar showed up the other day too…

531
00:27:18,937 --> 00:27:20,972
-Really?
-Yeah. I fought it.

532
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:22,807
They are strong!

533
00:27:22,874 --> 00:27:26,144
But I gave them the good ol' right hook!

534
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:28,113
And was able to drive them back.

535
00:27:28,179 --> 00:27:31,049
And then with my pride,
the "Left Straight",

536
00:27:31,116 --> 00:27:33,785
I made sure they didn't come back.

537
00:27:33,852 --> 00:27:36,454
If you install a right-turn signal
at that intersection,

538
00:27:36,521 --> 00:27:37,922
there won't be any traffic jams.

539
00:27:37,989 --> 00:27:40,258
Then, you can sleep for ten more minutes.

540
00:27:40,325 --> 00:27:42,027
Please come check it out.

541
00:27:42,093 --> 00:27:44,562
When can you come? When are you free?

542
00:27:44,629 --> 00:27:46,531
-Well…
-When is it?

543
00:27:46,598 --> 00:27:48,700
You are quite busy, I see.

544
00:27:49,267 --> 00:27:51,836
Every party member had the same schedule.

545
00:27:52,404 --> 00:27:54,572
And Kobayakawa staff have a rule.

546
00:27:54,639 --> 00:27:59,778
When they come to Chiba,
they always eat at Suzuran Hamburg.

547
00:27:59,844 --> 00:28:00,945
SUZURAN HAMBURG AS USUAL

548
00:28:01,746 --> 00:28:03,081
So, an ambush.

549
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:08,253
The secretary, Kiuchi, appears.

550
00:28:14,225 --> 00:28:15,560
Oh, sorry.

551
00:28:15,627 --> 00:28:16,761
It's okay.

552
00:29:03,208 --> 00:29:05,577
Welcome. Please choose any seat.

553
00:29:20,191 --> 00:29:21,793
Sir, is this yours?

554
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:23,528
Right!

555
00:29:24,662 --> 00:29:25,830
Thank you.

556
00:29:52,023 --> 00:29:53,291
And so…

557
00:29:53,358 --> 00:29:56,694
the shady money disappeared.

558
00:29:57,929 --> 00:30:00,098
So what was handed out instead?

559
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:03,301
Remains of dreams.

560
00:30:03,802 --> 00:30:06,838
I'm asking you,
what are you talking about?

561
00:30:06,905 --> 00:30:09,641
I thought hard about it,

562
00:30:10,608 --> 00:30:14,412
but I don't know why
they handed me this stuff.

563
00:30:15,413 --> 00:30:17,348
Old lottery tickets?

564
00:30:17,415 --> 00:30:21,119
If you're short of money, tell me!

565
00:30:21,186 --> 00:30:23,421
I have no idea what you are saying.

566
00:30:23,488 --> 00:30:25,190
Just spit it out already!

567
00:30:25,256 --> 00:30:26,324
I…

568
00:30:27,425 --> 00:30:30,028
I handed out the envelopes I got
from the Secretary General.

569
00:30:32,797 --> 00:30:37,569
The party staff divided the cash
in my room,

570
00:30:37,635 --> 00:30:40,004
and there was no problem then.

571
00:30:40,071 --> 00:30:43,708
The money vanished
only in Chiba District 17.

572
00:30:43,775 --> 00:30:46,778
I did my job just as I always do!

573
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:50,315
I didn't touch or look inside
the envelopes.

574
00:30:51,883 --> 00:30:54,752
Someone posted on FaceNote…

575
00:30:54,819 --> 00:30:58,857
"Party leadership isn't supporting
Kobayakawa Jr."

576
00:30:59,924 --> 00:31:03,328
"This is how they tell people
not to vote for him."

577
00:31:03,828 --> 00:31:06,331
Such rumors are spreading.

578
00:31:06,397 --> 00:31:07,565
What a disaster!

579
00:31:07,632 --> 00:31:08,967
I'm sorry.

580
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:11,035
-Did you do it?
-I didn't, but…

581
00:31:11,769 --> 00:31:13,304
I'm sure it's my fault.

582
00:31:14,005 --> 00:31:16,674
I have no idea, but I'm sure…

583
00:31:18,176 --> 00:31:20,111
-Probably…
-Which is it?

584
00:31:20,178 --> 00:31:22,981
Enough. Call Taniguchi.

585
00:31:23,047 --> 00:31:26,017
Explain it was a mix-up.

586
00:31:26,084 --> 00:31:29,287
Do we give the seasonal greetings again?

587
00:31:29,354 --> 00:31:30,421
Fool!

588
00:31:31,389 --> 00:31:34,259
We can't give out
secret cash during the election.

589
00:31:34,325 --> 00:31:36,194
You'll have to beg them to help!

590
00:31:36,261 --> 00:31:37,662
I understand!

591
00:31:40,765 --> 00:31:43,201
Are you sure he didn't do it?

592
00:31:44,202 --> 00:31:45,870
That man is unable to tell lies.

593
00:31:45,937 --> 00:31:48,673
Then someone must have

594
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,775
switched the contents somewhere.

595
00:31:52,977 --> 00:31:54,879
Who did it?

596
00:32:13,564 --> 00:32:15,500
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

597
00:32:31,215 --> 00:32:33,418
I saw heaven.

598
00:32:34,085 --> 00:32:35,920
That's too early.

599
00:32:35,987 --> 00:32:39,757
I wanted to see you in a wedding dress.

600
00:32:40,525 --> 00:32:42,994
Probably can't do that in this era.

601
00:32:44,429 --> 00:32:45,763
Yeah.

602
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:49,233
You've been like this
since you were small.

603
00:32:50,601 --> 00:32:54,372
This house is dear to me,

604
00:32:54,439 --> 00:32:55,807
but to you,

605
00:32:57,075 --> 00:32:59,577
it's like a chain.

606
00:33:02,146 --> 00:33:04,749
You only live once.

607
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,121
I'll leave this house

608
00:33:10,188 --> 00:33:12,457
to you.

609
00:33:14,058 --> 00:33:17,862
You can even sell it. Do what you like.

610
00:33:23,368 --> 00:33:29,273
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

611
00:33:48,626 --> 00:33:50,528
-What? You'll never hit.
-It seems hard.

612
00:33:51,329 --> 00:33:52,997
-It's never a win.
-Really?

613
00:33:53,865 --> 00:33:56,034
-I've never eaten this before.
-Really?

614
00:33:56,100 --> 00:33:58,269
-I'm curious.
-I always have this.

615
00:34:01,406 --> 00:34:03,274
Sorry about yesterday.

616
00:34:05,410 --> 00:34:09,447
I started this myself, knowing
it would likely fail, but I lost my nerve.

617
00:34:12,950 --> 00:34:15,286
This was my Bible in middle school.

618
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:19,390
Rousseau is a strange person
with many odd points,

619
00:34:19,457 --> 00:34:21,559
but I liked that he didn't lie.

620
00:34:22,126 --> 00:34:24,429
I haven't opened it in 15 years,
but I still remember a lot.

621
00:34:24,996 --> 00:34:27,665
You sure read hard books.

622
00:34:27,732 --> 00:34:30,935
Back then. Otherwise,
I only read English study books.

623
00:34:31,636 --> 00:34:32,703
Like Murphy.

624
00:34:47,185 --> 00:34:50,221
Miyabi! Miyabi! Wait…

625
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:53,558
You look super smart right now.

626
00:34:54,192 --> 00:34:55,059
What?

627
00:35:13,544 --> 00:35:15,913
Won't they say I'm showing off my English?

628
00:35:15,980 --> 00:35:17,949
Better than being thought of
as a stupid woman!

629
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:34,031
HER ENGLISH IS PRETTY NATURAL
GOOD PRONUNCIATION

630
00:35:34,098 --> 00:35:35,266
Hello?

631
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:39,070
If you're in Chiba right now,
I have good material for you.

632
00:35:40,872 --> 00:35:42,073
A screenshot

633
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:45,409
of a FaceNote post deleted last night.

634
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:48,346
It seems it was deleted, but what is this?

635
00:35:48,412 --> 00:35:49,580
Nothing…

636
00:35:51,315 --> 00:35:53,417
Have there been bribery acts
like this in the past?

637
00:35:54,852 --> 00:35:56,487
No, I really…

638
00:35:56,554 --> 00:35:58,489
This time I only got lottery tickets,

639
00:35:58,556 --> 00:36:00,625
and expired ones at that.

640
00:36:00,691 --> 00:36:01,859
Not cash vouchers.

641
00:36:01,926 --> 00:36:05,296
"Only" lottery tickets "this time."

642
00:36:06,664 --> 00:36:08,232
What about before?

643
00:36:08,299 --> 00:36:11,135
Elections are more favorable
than you think

644
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:13,304
when you have money.

645
00:36:13,371 --> 00:36:16,007
That's why old politics are being upheld.

646
00:36:16,073 --> 00:36:17,408
-Yeah!
-That's right!

647
00:36:17,975 --> 00:36:20,611
We must change that system.

648
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:21,979
Speak English!

649
00:36:22,046 --> 00:36:24,382
Can't you talk without a script?

650
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:40,865
MIYABI SPEAKING ENGLISH

651
00:36:40,932 --> 00:36:43,868
MIYABI IS SO COOL
SEEMS SHE'S ACTUALLY SMART?

652
00:36:43,935 --> 00:36:46,270
People don't exist
for the sake of the nation…

653
00:36:49,473 --> 00:36:50,875
…nation for the people.

654
00:36:50,942 --> 00:36:54,178
Mr. Hachimaki also borrowed money
to run, it seems.

655
00:36:55,513 --> 00:36:58,316
I listened to his speeches.
He made some good points.

656
00:36:58,382 --> 00:36:59,684
I see.

657
00:36:59,750 --> 00:37:01,919
He doesn't stand out at all though.

658
00:37:02,954 --> 00:37:05,423
Because laws are insufficient,

659
00:37:05,489 --> 00:37:09,160
we often can't help people in trouble.

660
00:37:09,227 --> 00:37:12,897
Some people can't be helped
unless we work on legislation.

661
00:37:12,964 --> 00:37:15,399
That's why I, a lawyer,

662
00:37:15,466 --> 00:37:17,101
chose to enter politics.

663
00:37:20,871 --> 00:37:21,806
Well…

664
00:37:22,974 --> 00:37:24,375
Let's talk policy.

665
00:37:24,442 --> 00:37:28,879
The Justice Ministry has a budget
for rehabilitating offenders,

666
00:37:28,946 --> 00:37:32,250
but not for victims' mental care
and supporting their daily lives.

667
00:37:32,316 --> 00:37:35,753
3 DAYS UNTIL VOTING

668
00:37:36,687 --> 00:37:38,656
Each of you

669
00:37:38,723 --> 00:37:41,559
has in yourself
a desire to improve society,

670
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:43,261
and we'll build a path together.

671
00:37:43,327 --> 00:37:44,428
That's an election.

672
00:37:46,130 --> 00:37:48,666
I want to smash, here and now,

673
00:37:48,733 --> 00:37:52,169
the system where more money
gives an advantage!

674
00:37:52,236 --> 00:37:53,371
Nice!

675
00:37:55,740 --> 00:37:58,743
Please give me your vote!

676
00:37:58,809 --> 00:38:01,846
Thank you, thank you.

677
00:38:02,446 --> 00:38:04,448
It must be tough in this heat, everyone.

678
00:38:05,383 --> 00:38:07,351
Don't push yourselves too hard.

679
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:09,553
Thank you.

680
00:38:10,821 --> 00:38:13,090
I left my own district to come here.

681
00:38:14,625 --> 00:38:16,927
The things you do for your kids!

682
00:38:19,697 --> 00:38:21,332
-Your seat is over there.
-Yes.

683
00:38:22,800 --> 00:38:24,001
-Sir.
-Yeah?

684
00:38:24,769 --> 00:38:25,936
Hayate says

685
00:38:26,537 --> 00:38:30,141
he wants to decline your support speech.

686
00:38:30,207 --> 00:38:31,142
What?

687
00:38:31,709 --> 00:38:34,512
He doesn't want favoritism
between siblings.

688
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,248
What is he thinking?

689
00:38:39,083 --> 00:38:41,052
He's the endorsed candidate!

690
00:38:41,118 --> 00:38:42,653
Why would he do that?

691
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:46,223
If he gets both money and a speech too,

692
00:38:46,290 --> 00:38:47,925
it would be unfair to his sister.

693
00:38:50,594 --> 00:38:51,962
The money was stolen.

694
00:38:54,532 --> 00:38:56,167
It was never given out.

695
00:38:58,235 --> 00:38:59,170
What?

696
00:38:59,236 --> 00:39:02,606
And safe and secure disaster prevention!

697
00:39:05,876 --> 00:39:08,446
With these three pillars,

698
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:11,248
I'll work as a member of the Kokuji Party

699
00:39:11,315 --> 00:39:16,287
to create a new, stronger Nipponia,
that will stand its ground!

700
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:23,461
I'll talk to him directly.
Where is he now?

701
00:39:24,762 --> 00:39:27,932
Sir! There's a new article.
Bribery suspicion.

702
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:32,036
SUSPICION OF ELECTION BRIBERY
IN CHIBA 17?

703
00:39:32,103 --> 00:39:34,905
DID THE BROTHER FAIL TO BUY VOTES?

704
00:39:51,422 --> 00:39:54,892
Three days before the vote,
an article suspecting bribery came out.

705
00:39:54,959 --> 00:39:57,928
Do you think it affected voters?

706
00:39:57,995 --> 00:39:59,697
As a matter of fact,

707
00:40:00,731 --> 00:40:03,701
I can say I committed no such crime.

708
00:40:04,668 --> 00:40:06,237
On top of that, the reason I lost,

709
00:40:07,037 --> 00:40:09,206
perhaps, is because I was a candidate

710
00:40:09,874 --> 00:40:11,675
without my own opinions.

711
00:40:13,844 --> 00:40:17,348
I got a seat through
proportional representation. So…

712
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:20,985
I'll rethink what kind of politician
I want to be.

713
00:40:21,051 --> 00:40:23,354
Independent newcomer Miyabi Kobayakawa

714
00:40:23,421 --> 00:40:27,091
defeated Kokuji Party newcomer
Hayate Kobayakawa by 210 votes.

715
00:40:27,158 --> 00:40:30,461
You have won this first battle.
Can you tell us your thoughts?

716
00:40:30,961 --> 00:40:32,997
English is fine too.

717
00:40:33,063 --> 00:40:34,532
Maybe next time.

718
00:40:36,867 --> 00:40:38,235
First,

719
00:40:38,302 --> 00:40:42,206
I apologize to Mr. Hachimaki,
who ran in the same district.

720
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:43,908
-Mr. Hachimaki?
-Yes.

721
00:40:44,475 --> 00:40:45,810
She's apologizing.

722
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:51,682
Our sibling uproar
probably got in his way.

723
00:40:52,483 --> 00:40:53,517
I'm sorry.

724
00:40:53,584 --> 00:40:54,752
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA - CHIBA 17

725
00:40:55,419 --> 00:40:57,555
People talk about winning and losing,

726
00:40:57,621 --> 00:41:00,658
but democracy isn't just majority rule.

727
00:41:01,325 --> 00:41:03,427
It's not about winning or losing. Right?

728
00:41:03,928 --> 00:41:05,362
What matters is

729
00:41:05,963 --> 00:41:09,133
finding a happiness everyone can share,

730
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:12,503
and elections are the process for it.

731
00:41:14,472 --> 00:41:17,908
I've become the representative
of District 17.

732
00:41:18,576 --> 00:41:20,811
Not only for those who voted for me,

733
00:41:20,878 --> 00:41:22,913
but for everyone who voted,

734
00:41:22,980 --> 00:41:26,684
including those who voted
for Mr. Hachimaki.

735
00:41:26,750 --> 00:41:28,118
I'll honor all your wishes,

736
00:41:28,185 --> 00:41:29,487
as much as I can,

737
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,655
as I go into national politics.

738
00:41:32,389 --> 00:41:33,791
Thank you.

739
00:42:01,652 --> 00:42:03,354
Congratulations.

740
00:42:04,955 --> 00:42:05,723
Here.

741
00:42:06,991 --> 00:42:08,492
A little gift.

742
00:42:08,559 --> 00:42:09,393
Huh?

743
00:42:10,227 --> 00:42:11,328
Are you sure?

744
00:42:11,395 --> 00:42:13,430
I got a mountain of them.

745
00:42:14,265 --> 00:42:15,466
I would throw it away.

746
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:19,403
If I…

747
00:42:20,104 --> 00:42:21,672
should leave the house…

748
00:42:21,739 --> 00:42:23,941
What are you saying? It's fine.

749
00:42:24,008 --> 00:42:26,310
You can just live there.
It's close by too.

750
00:42:29,446 --> 00:42:30,848
More importantly,

751
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:33,651
I have a proposal for you.

752
00:42:36,787 --> 00:42:38,656
Join the Kokuji Party.

753
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:50,200
Mr. Natsume.

754
00:42:50,267 --> 00:42:52,303
I came to greet you.

755
00:42:52,369 --> 00:42:53,671
SECRETARY
YAYOI KISARAGI

756
00:42:53,737 --> 00:42:56,073
Secretary?
Weren't you an election consultant?

757
00:42:56,140 --> 00:42:58,742
I quit that and became Miyabi's secretary.

758
00:42:59,610 --> 00:43:00,911
I see.

759
00:43:01,545 --> 00:43:03,180
We won.

760
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:07,051
Who would have thought she would win
just by being able to speak English?

761
00:43:07,117 --> 00:43:08,319
Just?

762
00:43:09,253 --> 00:43:10,988
Our Miyabi

763
00:43:11,055 --> 00:43:13,891
looked more like
a new wind to the voters, I guess.

764
00:43:16,293 --> 00:43:17,795
By the way…

765
00:43:18,796 --> 00:43:21,765
Does the safe
in the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office

766
00:43:21,832 --> 00:43:24,501
also hold losing lottery tickets?

767
00:43:25,736 --> 00:43:27,304
Well, I don't know.

768
00:43:28,439 --> 00:43:30,507
I'm glad we had a fair fight.

769
00:43:34,411 --> 00:43:36,580
We should thank the great thief.

770
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:45,990
I hope to see you again.

771
00:43:47,791 --> 00:43:48,993
Likewise.

772
00:44:02,039 --> 00:44:02,973
Next episode!

773
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:06,543
A storm of fake news and
malicious comments ravages the Internet!

774
00:44:06,610 --> 00:44:10,147
Tracing the source reveals
how money controls the system.

775
00:44:10,214 --> 00:44:14,018
If you can make money writing lies online,
you would do it, right?

776
00:44:14,084 --> 00:44:14,918
Would you do it?

777
00:44:14,985 --> 00:44:15,819
You wouldn't?

778
00:44:15,886 --> 00:44:16,920
I wouldn't.

779
00:44:16,987 --> 00:44:20,024
Are you okay, Nipponia?
Hang in there, Nipponia!

780
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:21,992
The bait has been thrown in.

781
00:44:22,059 --> 00:44:24,595
Now who will be caught by it?!

782
00:44:25,095 --> 00:44:28,432
I'm actually pretty angry.

783
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:29,967
Subtitle translation by: Quang N.N.
